  "worked_solution": "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=2$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7t & \\ge 19 \\\\ 7\\cdot 2 & \\ge 19 \\\\ 14 & \\ge 19\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=2$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=2$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=3$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7t & \\ge 19 \\\\ 7\\cdot 3 & \\ge 19 \\\\ 21 & \\ge 19\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=3$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=3$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=4$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7t & \\ge 19 \\\\ 7\\cdot 4 & \\ge 19 \\\\ 28 & \\ge 19\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=4$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=4$ **satisfies** this inequality.",
